<div class="autoscroll"><table class="list periodic-time-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Unit</th><th>Plan / Target</th><th>Actual</th><th>Deviation</th><th>Deviation Calculation</th><th>Deviation %</th><th>Contributing Tickets</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><% TicketJourneyPeriodicTime::METRICS.each do |key, (label, unit, direction)| %><% entry = report[:metrics][key] %>
    <tr><th><%= label %> <%= performance_tip(periodic_time_metric_tip(key)) %></th>
      <td><%= unit %></td>
      <td><%= periodic_time_number(entry[:plan], key) %></td><td><%= periodic_time_link(periodic_time_number(entry[:actual], key), key, ids) %></td>
      <td><%= periodic_time_link(periodic_time_deviation(key, entry), key, ids, class: periodic_time_class(key, entry)) %></td>
      <td><%= direction == :plan_minus_actual ? 'P−A' : 'A−P' %></td>
      <td class="<%= periodic_time_class(key, entry) %>"><%= entry[:deviation].nil? || entry[:deviation][:percent].nil? ? 'N/A' : "#{performance_number(entry[:deviation][:percent])}%" %></td>
      <td><%= periodic_time_link(entry[:rows].size, key, ids) %></td>
    </tr>
  <% end %></tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="performance-weight-note">P = Plan / Target. A = Actual. Cost and completed-expected owner hours compare matching ticket sets. Hover or focus the information icons for populations and time windows. CW/h uses the matching full expectation portfolio. Other Work's raw P−A is <%= periodic_time_number(report[:metrics]['other_hours'][:deviation]&.fetch(:value), 'other_hours') %> h. Favorable Extra Work is assessed separately at period end. Zero-plan percentages are <span style="white-space:nowrap">N/A.</span></p>
